    "author": "DDL095 <sealgod@qq.com>",
    "committer": "DDL095 <sealgod@qq.com>",
    "message": "v0.99.34: deterministic per-contrast GSEA seeding (upstream seed regression)\n\nclusterProfiler 4.19.3 switched GSEA() to the enrichit engine, and in\n4.20.0 (Bioconductor 3.23) the seed argument of GSEA() is silently\ndropped: it lands in ... and is never forwarded to\nenrichit::gsea_gson(), so the multilevel permutation engine draws a\nfresh seed from the worker R RNG on every call. Combined with\nfuture_lapply(future.seed = TRUE) deriving its worker seed stream from\nthe main-session RNG state at call time, re-running the same data could\nflip borderline pathways across the significance cutoff (observed\np-value drift up to +/-0.016), reproducing the publicly reported\n\"same code, different pathway counts\" issue.\n\nFix in R/04_calculation.R:\n- batch_calc_gsea() gains a seed argument (default 123; NULL restores\n  native engine sampling)\n- .derive_task_seed() maps (seed, alphabetical rank of contrast id) to\n  a per-contrast seed, so results are independent of workers/chunk_size\n- Seeds are derived in the main process and passed to future workers as\n  a plain named integer vector; workers apply withr::local_seed()\n  (restores RNG state on exit, per reviewer guidance against bare\n  set.seed()) and also forward the seed to GSEA(), which becomes\n  effective natively once clusterProfiler >= 4.21.1 restores it\n- The effective seed is recorded in metadata$parameters$seed\n\nTests: tests/testthat/test-batch-calc-gsea-seed.R pins cross-run\nreproducibility and worker-count independence (11 assertions).\n\nNEWS.md documents the fix and the one-time result shift vs pre-fix\ncapsules. Verified: R CMD check 0 ERROR / 0 WARNING; BiocCheck 0 ERRORS\n/ 0 WARNINGS.\n",
    "time": 1787082732
  },
